<title>POLAND: BRE, Pictet fund to be launched April 9.</title>
<headline>BRE, Pictet fund to be launched April 9.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A closed investment fund owned by the Polish  Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA and Swiss Pictet et Cie bank will start operations on April 9, BRE said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;On Wednesday, April 9, the fund will begin operations,&quot; BRE's spokeswoman Alicja Kos told Reuters.</p>
<p>The fund, registered in Luxembourg, will invest in unlisted companies and in participation units of the Polish mass privatisation programme.</p>
<p>Kos said the fund would be managed by Famco SA company, in which BRE and Pictet have 50 percent each. The fund's initial capital will amount to at least $25 million, she said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
